# EVERY COMPOSITIONAL ELEMENT OF BPMN THIS EMISSION WITHHOLDS, AND THE GROUND THE AXIS CLAIM
# SURVIVES IT ON. One row per withholding, and exactly one of the two grounds is filled.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ IT EXISTS BECAUSE A LAW COULD NOT TELL TWO WITHHOLDINGS APART, AND THE MOMENT THE MAPPING
#    IMPROVED IT ACCUSED THE IMPROVEMENT. `diagrams/notation.sqlc`'s ceded law reads a withheld
#    element on the COMPOSITION axis as a gap in the one axis this model claims whole, which is
#    right when nothing covers the fact and wrong when a BETTER element does. Withdrawing
#    `subProcess` in favour of `childLaneSet` fired it, and the finding was in the law rather than
#    in the emission.
#
# ⭐⭐ SO THE AXIS IS STILL WHOLE, AND NOW IT IS WHOLE FOR A STATED REASON. The claim was never
#    *every compositional ELEMENT is spent*; it is *every compositional FACT is covered*. An
#    element may sit in the withheld column only when a spent one carries what it carried, and
#    naming which one is what turns that from an excuse into a checkable sentence.
#
# ⛔ THE REPLACEMENT MUST ITSELF BE SPENT, or this relation launders a gap into a citation. That is
#   the arm of the law worth probing, not the existence of the row.
#
# ⭐⭐⭐ AND THE SECOND GROUND IS NOT AN EXCUSE, IT IS THE BOUNDARY CLAIM GETTING WEAKER AND SAYING
#    SO. `no_such_fact` means BPMN offers a compositional element THIS MODEL HAS NOTHING TO PUT IN,
#    which is not a gap in our coverage: it is the place where BPMN is the wider of the two. The
#    law admits it and the report COUNTS it, because *on composition this model is the finer* is
#    a claim that has to be allowed to shrink. ⛔ Reclassifying such a row onto another axis to
#    make the law pass would be re-taxonomising BPMN to protect a sentence, which is the failure
#    `group` was rescued from and not one to repeat.
#
# ⛔⛔ EXACTLY ONE OF `superseded_by` AND `no_such_fact` IS FILLED, the schema's own `<>` idiom.
#   A row with both would be saying the fact is carried and does not exist.
#
# ⚠️ A `VALUES` LITERAL, for the same reason `diagrams/graphs.sqlc` is one: derived from the
#   emission it could only ever report replacements that already happened correctly, and never a
#   row somebody wrote down and did not carry out.
-- the mapping's own history: what was tried, what replaced it, and where BPMN is simply wider.
SELECT * FROM (VALUES
  ('subProcess'::text, 'childLaneSet'::text, NULL::boolean,
   '⭐ A LOCAL FUSION IS A PARTITION, NOT AN ACTIVITY. `subProcess` is a flow node, so it collapses layer to document exactly as `calledElement` does; a nested lane keeps the key `(filing, layer)`. Measured: 10 of 27 parts are local, and every one of them left the flattening when this changed'::text),
  ('partitionElementRef', NULL, true,
   '⭐⭐⭐ THE ONLY PLACE BPMN IS THE FINER OF THE TWO, AND IT WAS TESTED BEFORE IT WAS FILED. `tLane` carries this for WHAT the partition is BY, per lane. The nearest filler is the absorber BUFFER and it fails: 14 filings here have two or more layers sharing one buffer, up to FOUR lanes on `capacity` in one process, so pointing at it would assert a partition the model does not make. A layer''s identity is its NAME and nothing else, so there is no element to point at')
) AS s(element, superseded_by, no_such_fact, why)
